warning[SC0402]: this may use a value after it was freed
   ╭─[ an_unsequenced_free_and_use_is_not_proved.c:5:13 ]
   │
 4 │     int *p = malloc(4);
   │              ────┬────  
   │                  ╰────── allocated here
 5 │     int x = *p + (free(p), 0);
   │             ────────┬┬──────  
   │                     ╰───────── used here, perhaps after the free
   │                      │        
   │                      ╰──────── freed here
───╯
  = note: C17 6.5 p3 leaves these unsequenced, so one order frees first and the other does not
  = note: this check belongs to safety level 1
  = note: this could not be proven; `--deny-unknown` makes it an error
